            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0674" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/371: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-16T19:00:00+02:00">March 16, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 16—3:36 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. The Minister now informs me that the <hi rendition="#italic">Maiotis</hi> has
                    been ordered by wireless to return at once to Piraeus. He explained that as the
                    fugitive has no papers to enter Egypt he must have arranged some further
                    stratagem which this action may forestall.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
